{"schema":1,"id":"agentic-mermaid","title":"What does a Mermaid verifier check?","lang":"en","sources":["https://github.com/adewale/agentic-mermaid","https://www.npmjs.com/package/agentic-mermaid/v/0.5.1","https://github.com/adewale/agentic-mermaid/blob/main/AGENT_NATIVE.md"],"settings":[{"id":"edit","label":"The agent’s first edit","default":"swapped","options":[{"value":"swapped","label":"Labels yes to Database"},{"value":"missing","label":"Leaves out branch labels"},{"value":"complete","label":"Labels yes to Reply"}]}],"answer":"Verify fails a diagram that Agentic Mermaid’s renderer cannot draw, warns about structural gaps such as an unlabelled branch out of a decision, and leaves what the labels mean unchecked","checks":[{"question":"The agent writes the second edge as A -->|no| D, and D appears nowhere else in the source. What does verify(flow) report?","answer":"ok: true and no warnings. Mermaid creates D where it is first used, as a rectangle labelled D, so the diagram draws and both exits of the decision carry labels. That the agent meant Database is the kind of thing verify leaves unchecked."},{"question":"Starting from the right diagram, the agent adds a second, unlabelled edge from Cached to Database: A --> C. Which edge does the warning name?","answer":"A->C#1. It is the second edge from A to C, so its count is 1, while the labelled edge to Database keeps A->C#0. One DECISION_BRANCH_UNLABELED warning, and ok stays true."},{"question":"Draw Cached as a rectangle, A[Cached], and leave both edges unlabelled. Does the verifier warn?","answer":"No: ok: true with no warnings. DECISION_BRANCH_UNLABELED is about the exits of a decision diamond, and a rectangle is not a decision, so there is nothing for it to flag."},{"question":"The agent deletes the whole line for the edge to Database and leaves the edge to Reply unlabelled: A{Cached} --> B[Reply]. How many warnings?","answer":"None: ok: true with no warnings. The warning is for a decision with two or more exits, and Cached now has one, so its one unlabelled exit is not flagged."}],"cases":[{"values":{"edit":"swapped"},"name":"The agent’s first edit: Labels yes to Database","duration":111.833,"paper":"#123a63","steps":[{"step":"source","title":"This diagram sends a cache hit to the database","line":"does Agentic Mermaid’s verifier accept this diagram?","caption":"A cache hit follows yes to Database, while no leads straight to Reply. This reverses the intended cache behavior. Agentic Mermaid’s verify(flow) returns a report about the source. Will it accept this diagram?","start":0,"end":12.4,"hold":2.3,"state":{},"changed":{},"picture":"Flowchart: 3 nodes, 2 links; Code, 3 lines.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                                                               ┌────────────────────────────┐\n│                                                               │                            │\n│                                                               │ graph LR                   │\n│                                                               │ A{Cached} -->|no| B[Reply] │\n│  ▌  ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐  │ A -->|yes| C[Database]     │\n│  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  │                            │\n│  ▌  ││ ┌─────────────┐│ ││ ││││ ││ ││ ││ ││││ ││ ││ ││ ││ ││  └────────────────────────────┘\n│  ──────│─────────────│─────┌────┐─────────┌───────────┐─────\n│  ──────│─────────────│─────││───│─────────│───────────│─────\n│  ──────│─────────────│─────└────┘─────────└───────────┘─────\n│  ▌  ││ ││ │───────││ ││ ││ ││││ ││ ││ ││ ││││ ││ ││ ││ ││ ││\n│  ──────│─────────────│─────┌────┐─────────┌───────────┐─────\n│  ──────│─────────────│─────│────│─────────│───────────│─────\n│  ▌  ││ ││ ││ ││││ ││ ││ ││ └────┘│ ││ ││ │└───────────┘││ ││\n│  ──────└─────────────┘──────────────────────────────────────\n│  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│  ▌  └┘ └┘ └┘ └┘└┘ └┘ └┘ └┘ └┘└┘ └┘ └┘ └┘ └┘└┘ └┘ └┘ └┘ └┘ └┘\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│"},{"step":"verify","title":"verify(flow) returns ok: true, with no warnings","line":"The dot follows the yes edge as drawn: from Cached to Database.","caption":"The source renders and both decision exits carry labels, so the report has no warnings. Yet its yes path reaches Database. taskCorrectness: not-checked names the boundary: Verify fails a diagram that Agentic Mermaid’s renderer cannot draw, warns about structural gaps such as an unlabelled branch out of a decision, and leaves what the labels mean unchecked.","start":12.4,"end":33.4,"hold":14.667,"state":{"warnings":[],"taskCorrectness":"not-checked","swappedWarnings":0,"walks":[{"step":"verify","from":"A","to":"C","edge":"edge:A->C#0"}]},"changed":{"warnings":{"after":[]},"taskCorrectness":{"after":"not-checked"},"swappedWarnings":{"after":0},"walks":{"after":[{"step":"verify","from":"A","to":"C","edge":"edge:A->C#0"}]}},"picture":"Flowchart: 3 nodes, 2 links; Code, 3 lines; Code, 3 lines. Yes, to Database: Cached → Database: yes. New in this step: Code, 3 lines.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                                                               ┌────────────────────────────┐\n│                                                               │                            │\n│                                                               │ graph LR                   │\n│                                                               │ A{Cached} -->|no| B[Reply] │\n│  ▌  ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐ ┌┐  │ A -->|yes| C[Database]     │\n│  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  │                            │\n│  ▌  ││ ┌─────────────┐│ ││ ││││ ││ ││ ││ ││││ ││ ││ ││ ││ ││  ┌────────────────────────────┐\n│  ──────│─────────────│─────┌────┐─────────┌───────────┐─────  │                            │\n│  ──────│─────────────│─────││───│─────────│───────────│─────  │ verify(flow).ok: true      │\n│  ──────│─────────────│─────└────┘─────────└───────────┘─────  │ warnings: 0                │\n│  ▌  ││ ││ │───────││ ││ ││ ││││ ││ ││ ││ ││││ ││ ││ ││ ││ ││  │ taskCorrectness: not-checked\n│  ──────│─────────────│─────┌────┐─────────┌───────────┐─────  └────────────────────────────┘\n│  ──────│─────────────│─────│────│─────────│───────────│─────\n│  ▌  ││ ││ ││ ││││ ││ ││ ││ └────┘│ ││ ││ │└───────────┘││ ││\n│  ──────└─────────────┘──────────────────────────────────────\n│  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│  ▌  └┘ └┘ └┘ └┘└┘ └┘ └┘ └┘ └┘└┘ └┘ └┘ └┘ └┘└┘ └┘ └┘ └┘ └┘ └┘\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│"},{"step":"broken","title":"Cut the end off an edge, and verify returns ok: false","line":"with no node at the end of its last arrow, can this source be drawn at all?","caption":"The last arrow has no destination. This pinned renderer cannot draw it, so RENDER_FAILED makes ok false; UNSUPPORTED_SYNTAX identifies the dangling edge. The failure establishes a rendering problem without needing to know what a cache should do.","start":33.4,"end":47.3,"hold":35.533,"state":{"warnings":[],"taskCorrectness":"not-checked","swappedWarnings":0,"walks":[{"step":"verify","from":"A","to":"C","edge":"edge:A->C#0"}],"broken":{"source":"graph LR\nA{Cached} -->|no| B[Reply]\nA -->|yes|","ok":false,"warnings":[{"code":"RENDER_FAILED","severity":"error"},{"code":"UNSUPPORTED_SYNTAX","severity":"warning","syntax":"flowchart_dangling_edge"}],"checks":{"renderability":"failed","taskCorrectness":"not-checked"}}},"changed":{"broken":{"after":{"source":"graph LR\nA{Cached} -->|no| B[Reply]\nA -->|yes|","ok":false,"warnings":[{"code":"RENDER_FAILED","severity":"error"},{"code":"UNSUPPORTED_SYNTAX","severity":"warning","syntax":"flowchart_dangling_edge"}],"checks":{"renderability":"failed","taskCorrectness":"not-checked"}}}},"picture":"Code, 3 lines; Code, 6 lines; 1 label. An edge with no end: 3: A -->|yes|. New in this step: Code, 6 lines; 1 label.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│          ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐         ┌────────────────────────────┐\n│          │                                          │         │ verify(flow).ok: false     │\n│          │ graph LR                                 │         │ warnings: 2                │\n│          │                                          │         │   RENDER_FAILED (error)    │\n│          │ A{Cached} -->|no| B[Reply]               │         │                            │\n│          ▌                                          │         │   UNSUPPORTED_SYNTAX (warning)\n│          ▌ A -->|yes|                               │         │ renderability: failed      │\n│          ▌                                          │         │ taskCorrectness: not-checked\n│          └──────────────────────────────────────────┘         └────────────────────────────┘\n│\n│    The renderer cannot draw this source: no picture\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│"},{"step":"flagged","title":"Delete both labels, and the verifier warns twice","line":"does a missing label turn ok false too?","caption":"DECISION_BRANCH_UNLABELED is the warning for a decision with two or more exits where one exit carries no label. Agentic Mermaid names an edge by its two ends and a count: A->C#0 is the first edge from A, Cached, to C, Database. The warnings identify the unlabelled paths to Reply and Database. The diagram still renders, so ok stays true. A missing label is structural information the verifier can detect; choosing the correct label needs task knowledge.","start":47.3,"end":75.8,"hold":51.2,"state":{"warnings":[],"taskCorrectness":"not-checked","swappedWarnings":0,"walks":[{"step":"verify","from":"A","to":"C","edge":"edge:A->C#0"}],"broken":{"source":"graph LR\nA{Cached} -->|no| B[Reply]\nA -->|yes|","ok":false,"warnings":[{"code":"RENDER_FAILED","severity":"error"},{"code":"UNSUPPORTED_SYNTAX","severity":"warning","syntax":"flowchart_dangling_edge"}],"checks":{"renderability":"failed","taskCorrectness":"not-checked"}},"flaggedWarnings":2},"changed":{"flaggedWarnings":{"after":2}},"picture":"Flowchart: 3 nodes, 2 links; Code, 3 lines; Code, 7 lines. Note: “A->B#0” beside Cached → Reply; “A->C#0” beside Cached → Database; flagged: Cached; Cached → Reply; and 1 more. New in this step: Flowchart: 3 nodes, 2 links; 2: A{Cached} --> B[Reply]; 3: A --> C[Database]; and 6 more.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│  ┌───┌┐──┌┐──┌┐──┌┐─┌┐──┌┐──┌┐──┌┐─┌┐──┌┐──┌┐──┌┐─┌┐──┌┐──┌┐  ┌───────────────────────────┐\n│  │   ││  ││  ││  ││ ││  ││  ││  ││ ││  ││  ││  ││ ││  ││  ││  │ graph LR                  │\n│  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  │                           │\n│  │   ││ ┌───────────────────┐│  ││ ││  ││  ││  ││ ││  ││  ││  │ A{Cached} --> B[Reply]    │\n│  ───────│─────────────────A->B#0────┌────────────────┐──────  │ A --> C[Database]         │\n│  ───────│───────────────────│───────│────────────────│──────  │                           │\n│  │   ││ │││  ││  ││ ││ ─────│───────│  ││  ││  ││ ││ │││  ││  └───────────────────────────┘\n│  ───────│───────────────────│───────└────────────────┘──────  ┌────────────────────────────┐\n│  │   ││ │││  │───────── ││  ││  ││ ││  ││  ││  ││ ││  ││  ││  │ verify(flow).ok: true      │\n│  ───────│───────────────────│───────┌────────────────┐──────  │ warnings: 2                │\n│  │   ││ │││  ││  ││ ││ ─────│───────│  ───────────││ │││  ││  │   DECISION_BRANCH_UNLABELED│\n│  ───────│───────────────────────────│────────────────│──────  │     edge A->B#0            │\n│  │   ││ │││  ││  ││ ││  ││A->C#0││ │└────────────────┘││  ││  │   DECISION_BRANCH_UNLABELED│\n│  ───────└───────────────────┘───────────────────────────────  │                            │\n│  │   ││  ││  ││  ││ ││  ││  ││  ││ ││  ││  ││  ││ ││  ││  ││  │     edge A->C#0            │\n│  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  │ taskCorrectness: not-checked\n│  └───└┘──└┘──└┘──└┘─└┘──└┘──└┘──└┘─└┘──└┘──└┘──└┘─└┘──└┘──└┘  └────────────────────────────┘\n│\n│\n│"},{"step":"meaning","title":"Label them the right way round: the report does not change","line":"The wrong diagram and the right one get the same report.","caption":"Two set_label edits put yes on the path to Reply and no on the path to Database. A hit now follows the intended route, but the report is identical to the backwards diagram’s. Distinguishing them needs a check that a cache hit reaches Reply without querying Database; this page describes that missing obligation rather than implementing it.","start":75.8,"end":97.2,"hold":79.933,"state":{"warnings":[],"taskCorrectness":"not-checked","swappedWarnings":0,"walks":[{"step":"verify","from":"A","to":"C","edge":"edge:A->C#0"},{"step":"meaning","from":"A","to":"B","edge":"edge:A->B#0"}],"broken":{"source":"graph LR\nA{Cached} -->|no| B[Reply]\nA -->|yes|","ok":false,"warnings":[{"code":"RENDER_FAILED","severity":"error"},{"code":"UNSUPPORTED_SYNTAX","severity":"warning","syntax":"flowchart_dangling_edge"}],"checks":{"renderability":"failed","taskCorrectness":"not-checked"}},"flaggedWarnings":2,"reports":{"wrong":{"ok":true,"warnings":0},"right":{"ok":true,"warnings":0}}},"changed":{"walks":{"before":[{"step":"verify","from":"A","to":"C","edge":"edge:A->C#0"}],"after":[{"step":"verify","from":"A","to":"C","edge":"edge:A->C#0"},{"step":"meaning","from":"A","to":"B","edge":"edge:A->B#0"}]},"reports":{"after":{"wrong":{"ok":true,"warnings":0},"right":{"ok":true,"warnings":0}}}},"picture":"Flowchart: 3 nodes, 2 links; Code, 3 lines; Code, 3 lines; Code, 3 lines. Yes, to Reply: Cached → Reply: yes. New in this step: Cached → Database: no; 2: A